      },
      [],
      "Introduces global gender issues through interdisciplinary, culturally situated, theoretically diverse, and policy-oriented perspectives. Students examine gender as a socio-political, religio-cultural, economic, and historical construct, and its intersections with other dimensions of identity. Through scholarly research and case studies, students analyze how gender inequalities are produced, experienced, negotiated, and challenged through systems of power and privilege and evaluate efforts to advance gender equity across global contexts.",
      []
    ]
